id: pm-rl-review107later
title: Triage the three later review threads outside the seven-finding round
description: "Follow up PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6x8fDn (duplicate public acceptance evidence), PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6x8fDs (fixed-result lifecycle sources), and PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6x8fDu (unreadable process birth identity). These arrived after the seven requested threads; preserve released compatibility and require independent regression/revert evidence before changes."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rl#107",review
created_at: "2026-10-30T13:55:27.424Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T06:49:22.781Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-rl-sequential
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-30T18:08:05.446Z",codex-agent,"Related stopping/identity diagnostic on untouched cd91de9: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"native child identity failure and PID reuse\" test/process.test.ts reports 1 test, 0 pass, 1 failure. The fixture expects Cannot establish trainer process identity but receives Trainer exceeded wall or staging allowance. The current full integration attempt flags the same test. This does not establish that the later stopTrainer thread has the same root cause; retain the identity and allowance evidence for triage without weakening the existing bounds."
  "2026-10-31T00:21:05.202Z",codex-agent,"The original native-child identity failure now passes: identity tools honor the supplied PATH instead of bypassing it with a platform installation path. With an empty PATH, a real child fails with process_identity_unavailable and is reaped. This fixes the observed fixture/lookup defect; the three later review threads remain separately tracked and unclosed."
  "2026-10-31T01:52:18.677Z","harness:claude-code","Fixed all three by hand on #107. (1) PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6x8fDu stopTrainer: an unreadable birth identity counts as stopped only when kill(pid, 0) reports ESRCH, and an unreadable identity after SIGKILL is not proof of stop. New assertion in controller-boundaries 'recovery stops only the exact live trainer' fails on revert (0/1). (2) PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6x8fDs fixed-result read path: the result must follow the plan, every collection Run and the candidate, via the shared fixedLifecycleArtifacts. New test 'fixed results created before their collection Run and candidate never promote' fails on revert (0/1). Legitimate recording always verifies Runs and candidate first, so no released result can have the old ordering. (3) PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6x8fDn: the stale public_node_and_bun copy now references docs/sequential-evaluation-evidence.json (same commit, snapshot and comparison, current evidence_digest). Also fixed: the 'git absent from PATH' CLI test and evaluation-plan.acceptance now link the platform identity tool, because the merged process-job fence needs getconf/ps (the test failed at e0fb7d9 with process_identity_unavailable)."
  "2026-10-31T03:58:12.469Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit round on 0a9a36c (4 minor), fixed by hand. (1) Git discovery validates only the .git marker, so standalone trackers below symlinked ancestors (macOS /var, linked /home) are no longer refused; a linked marker is still rl_state_path_invalid. The new checkpoint-artifacts test fails on revert. The durable-loop alias launch now resolves to the same shared authority (exit 0), and the second worktree still gets loop_launch_elsewhere. (2) Checkpoint-producing entry points (improver run, prefix meta recipes, prefix process fits) refuse checkpoint_storage_unsupported before any reservation, lease or receipt; the new mutation-preflight test fails when each of the three preflights is reverted separately. README documents the restriction. (3) The two sequential-evaluation tests start try right after setting PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS. (4) Card export and replay share citationOrder (UTF-8 bytes). It is unreachable today: native IDs are lowercase [a-z0-9-], pm rejects é and _, and 200k fuzzed pairs give identical code-unit and collation order. Unified to remove the latent mismatch. Suites: mutation-preflight + checkpoint-artifacts 44/44, policy-card replay 4/4, durable-loop alias 1/1; check (0 clones), docstring 499, lint, changelog pass."
  "2026-10-31T04:47:29.487Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit round on 342f21f (2 minor), fixed by hand. persistLmCheckpoint rebuilds the temporary and target paths from pmRoot right before link and rm, so a runtime or pm-rl component swapped for a link during the awaited write is refused. The new lm test 'checkpoint publication refuses a state directory swapped for a link during the write' fails on revert (0/1). The README and statePath docstring now name exactly what is refused: a linked root, linked directories below it and linked leaves; links above the root are permitted. lm 18/18; check (0 clones), docstring 499, lint, changelog pass."
  "2026-10-31T05:46:41.143Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit round on 2977fbc (3 minor), fixed by hand. (1) public_node_and_bun records per-runtime evidence_digests (node 0f81a4e5…, bun 99b141f7…, from docs/decision-evidence-validation.json public_input_roots) instead of one digest implying equivalence. (2) The stopTrainer identity-failure test injects the failure through both read (/proc on Linux) and exec (ps or PowerShell elsewhere). (3) The corpus refusal tests assert exactly one code per case: the state boundary deterministically preempts linked roots and parents, dangling links and roots below a file with rl_state_path_invalid; codes were measured per case before narrowing. Check (0 clones), lint, changelog pass; the affected tests pass."
  "2026-10-31T06:49:22.781Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit round on c7c44d1: the exported parseSequentialStopping now refuses null, undefined, primitives and arrays with eval_plan_invalid before Object.keys, instead of throwing TypeError. The strict-schema test covers all four guard operands and fails on revert (0/1). Check (0 clones), lint and changelog pass."
